{
  "title": "Split prep words that follow the food without a comma out of the item",
  "description": "Lines like '5 pears peeled and chopped', '3 eggs lightly beaten', '8 strawberries trimmed (hulled, quartered)' and '3 handfuls basil leaves roughly torn' keep the prep words in `item` ('pears peeled and chopped'), so the catalog doesn't resolve them: resolver step 4 only trims ', ...' clauses. \
Measured 2026-10-18: about 440 of the 5,395 once-seen unresolved names in the pipeline fixtures have this shape (heuristic: a prep word such as peeled/chopped/minced/sliced/beaten/trimmed/torn/cut/diced after the first word). \
Each costs calories and density, and the shopping category once the keyword categorizer goes (p3-catalog-close-category-gap). \
Fix in the parser (move the trailing prep phrase to `note`) or the resolver (try the name with a trailing prep phrase dropped), keeping names where the word is part of the food ('peeled tomatoes', 'cut green beans', 'chopped clams'). \
Rerun make ingredient-tests-update and make pipeline and commit the diffs; check make ingredient-catalog-audit for the coverage change.",
